                <head>No. 465<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>According to Hagerty’s diary President Eisenhower and Prime Minister Churchill
                    had a private conversation for three quarters of an hour in the President’s
                    office shortly after noon on June 25. No record of this conversation has been
                    found in Department of State files. (Eisenhower Library, James C. Hagerty
                    papers)</p>
            </div>
